[38;5;252m[1m## Fixes made[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Two changes to [38;5;10mtranslation/src/lib.rs[0m, both about faithfulness rather than logic:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mptr::copy_nonoverlapping[0m → the real [38;5;10mmemcpy[0m. [38;5;10mcp_stored[0m copies [38;5;10mLEN[0m bytes with no bounds check, so a truncated stored block makes the source range run over the destination; Rust calls that UB and aborted under [38;5;10mdebug_assertions[0m, while the C just does whatever glibc's [38;5;10mmemcpy[0m does.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10m.offset()[0m → [38;5;10m.wrapping_offset()[0m in the pointer walks that legitimately step one past the end of an object ([38;5;10mcp_stored[0m, [38;5;10mcp_block[0m, [38;5;10mcp_unfilter[0m, [38;5;10mcp_convert[0m, [38;5;10mcp_depalette[0m), matching the C's pointer arithmetic.[0m[0m
