[38;5;252m[1m## Inputs that cannot be compared[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Three classes are detected and skipped rather than asserted on, because the C reference has no defined answer:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- **Heap-content dependent.** [38;5;10mcp_stored[0m's unguarded [38;5;10mmemcpy[0m over-reads past [38;5;10mmalloc(datalen)[0m when a stored block is cut short. Each case is run twice per library with differently poisoned heaps; if C disagrees with itself the case is skipped. Only 2 of 4653 truncation cases and 0 of 3717 mutations fell into this bucket.[0m[0m
- **Live [38;5;10massert()[0m.** The reference [38;5;10m.so[0m built with the command in the task has no [38;5;10m-DNDEBUG[0m, so [38;5;10m__assert_fail[0m is linked in and malformed Huffman streams abort the process. The Rust elides asserts (per its own header comment), so tests avoid constructing invalid trees — the fixture generator only emits streams whose trees satisfy Kraft equality.[0m[0m
- **Non-terminating or wild-pointer C paths.** A chunk length of [38;5;10m0xFFFFFFF4[0m makes [38;5;10mcp_find[0m advance by zero and loop forever; a length above [38;5;10m0x7FFFFFF4[0m makes [38;5;10mcp_chunk[0m's [38;5;10mint offset[0m negative and moves [38;5;10mpng.p[0m ~2 GiB backwards into unmapped memory. Both are excluded, with the reason recorded at the exclusion site.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
One thing I did not verify: [38;5;10mcp_dynamic[0m's [38;5;10mlens[][0m is uninitialised stack in the C and zero-padded in the Rust. A corrupt stream whose first code-length symbol is 16 reads [38;5;10mlens[-1][0m, and there is no way to make Rust reproduce a particular C build's stack garbage. The padding is a deliberate hardening choice already documented in the Rust source.[0m[0m
